  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale-up of HIV-AIDS prevention, care and treatment services to 354 priority health zones targeting the general and key populations in the Democratic Republic of Congo - Congo (Democratic Republic) (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Congo (Democratic Republic), HIV, Ministry of Public Health, Hygiene and Social Security (MOH DRC)This program has the following goals: Contribute to the development of the country by decreasing transmission of HIV in individuals, families and communities (contribute to the decrease of 50% in new infections and mortality) in 354 targeted Health Zones.  Ensure global care and treatment of all TB/HIV co-infected patients in DRC. The objectives of this program are: Enrol 95% of TB/HIV co-infected patients on ART by 2017.  Reduce from 28.5% to 8% new infections in infants born to HIV positive mothers.  Reduce HIV related mortality in adults from 33/100,000 in 2014 to 17/100,000 in 2017</narrative>
  </description>
